# The list of expected unsupported tests (test/expected-unsupported.txt,
# #608) agrees with the REQUIRES and UNSUPPORTED lines of the tests: every
# test listed under a feature names it, and every test that names a feature
# with explicit entries is listed under it.
# RUN: %python %S/../mdir_lit.py %S/.. | FileCheck --check-prefix=LIST %s
# LIST: entries, {{[0-9]+}} tests, 0 problems
#
# The check of a configuration, on a suite of its own whose list differs
# from what its features leave unsupported: a warning on a run of the whole
# suite, also at the end of its log; an error with strict; nothing when the
# list agrees, or on a run of one test.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %lit -Dout=%t %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=WARN %s
# RUN: not %lit -Dout=%t -Dexpected_unsupported=strict %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=STRICT %s
# RUN: %lit -Dout=%t -Dfeatures=a,c,d -Dexpected_unsupported=strict %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=AGREE %s
# RUN: %lit -Dout=%t %S/Inputs/unsupported/runs.test 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ONE %s
# RUN: not %lit -Dout=%t -Dexpected_unsupported=maybe %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=BAD %s
#
# A shard compares its own tests, those that lit takes in the lexical order
# of their names, which a shard must ask for (D309): lit's default order
# follows the times recorded in each build tree, so the shards of two trees
# overlap and leave tests out.
# RUN: %lit -Dout=%t --num-shards=2 --run-shard=1 --order=lexical %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SHARD1 %s
# RUN: %lit -Dout=%t --num-shards=2 --run-shard=2 --order=lexical %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SHARD2 %s
# RUN: not %lit -Dout=%t --num-shards=2 --run-shard=1 %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ORDER %s
# RUN: env LIT_OPTS="--num-shards=2 --run-shard=2" not %lit -Dout=%t %S/Inputs/unsupported 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ORDER %s
# SHARD1: note: expected unsupported: 1 of 3 tests of shard 1/2
# SHARD1: unsupported but not expected: needs-c.test (without c)
# SHARD1-NEXT: expected unsupported but runs: runs.test
# SHARD2: note: expected unsupported: 2 of 2 tests of shard 2/2
# SHARD2-NOT: warning
# SHARD2: Total Discovered Tests: 5
# ORDER: fatal: a shard of the suite takes --order=lexical
# WARN: note: expected unsupported: 3 of 5 tests
# WARN: warning: the unsupported tests differ from test/expected-unsupported.txt:
# WARN-NEXT: unsupported but not expected: needs-c.test (without c)
# WARN-NEXT: expected unsupported but runs: runs.test
# WARN: Total Discovered Tests: 5
# WARN: lit: warning: the unsupported tests differ
# STRICT: fatal: the unsupported tests differ from test/expected-unsupported.txt:
# STRICT-NEXT: unsupported but not expected: needs-c.test (without c)
# AGREE: note: expected unsupported: 2 of 5 tests
# AGREE-NOT: warning
# AGREE: Total Discovered Tests: 5
# ONE-NOT: expected unsupported
# BAD: expected_unsupported must be check, strict, or off, not 'maybe'
